  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of dizziness and presyncope in the setting of known sick sinus syndrome (I49.5) and atherosclerotic heart disease (I25.10). Given the recent transient cerebral ischemic attack, Mobile Cardiac Telemetry monitoring (CPT 93229) is ordered to evaluate for potential arrhythmic causes of cerebral hypoperfusion and to optimize rate control. This continuous monitoring is medically necessary to identify the arrhythmia responsible for the transient cerebral ischemic attack and to guide management of the sick sinus syndrome."
